# Captured renders are evidence, not source — regenerate them with
# capture-render.mjs rather than tracking them.
#
# ⛔ `rig-canvas.png` in particular must NEVER be committed. It is a render of
# the REFERENCE rig's own output. D880 authorised porting the vertex-shader
# MECHANISM; it did not authorise keeping copies of the reference's rendered
# artwork, and KJC-4's surviving constraint ("study it, write our own, keep
# nothing") applies to imagery regardless — an image is an artistic work, a
# different asset class from a computer program.
*.png

# fidelity-compare.mjs's run-scoped output (Task 2) — imagery per the rule
# above, PLUS the intermediate compare.py --json stat blocks per rung, which
# are debug artefacts of a single run, not the tracked result. The tracked
# result is fidelity-baseline.json, one level up, outside this directory.
runs/
